Carl wrote:

> On Mar 15, 10:24 am, Derek Ray wrote:
>> Perhaps not elementals [...], but i'm definitely still leaning towards
>> the idea of increasing golem risk (ie. create a circumstance where there
>> is -no- safe way to polymorph more than one object per square) [...]
> 
> Perhaps I am misunderstanding you, but limiting polypiling to 1 object
> per square seems like it takes away the reward for all but those who
> can cast polymorph.

I think he meant that something different: if you want to ensure safety
polypiling (no golem creation!), then one item per pile is the limit. From
two items onwards, something bad can happen.

Plainly disallowing polymorphing larger stack would be counterintuitive on
the interface anyway, I think.

Your point on the Polymorph spell is valid: any attempt to make polypiling
more interesting (by making it more risky, for example) in this ways
discussed here, adds another source of grinding: single-item, spell-powered
poly ordeals. That's pretty bad, I think. Elsewhere, that would probably be
taken as an excuse to either remove or completely change the spell. (To be
honest, I find the idea of duplicating wand effects by spellbooks pretty
dubious in general.)

David


